\p{Sources (read-only clones, nothing built or run):}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|refs/rpylean~} — \<html:a>[href]{\verb~|https://github.com/Julian/rpylean~}{https://github.com/Julian/rpylean} at \code{\verb~|bbf354d3adbfe84d297ea2159cc707b48d96a90a~} (the arena pin, v2026.11.11, HEAD of the clone; 718 commits of history read). ~21 k lines of RPython, of which \code{\verb~|rpylean/machine.py~} (12 879 lines) is the kernel.}
\li{\code{\verb~|refs/tenet-jvm~} — \<html:a>[href]{\verb~|https://github.com/keithadler/tenet-jvm~}{https://github.com/keithadler/tenet-jvm}. The arena pins \code{\verb~|4cc6e20~} (v0.1.5); the clone's HEAD is \code{\verb~|53cf8a4~} (3 commits later). Unless stated otherwise, tenet-jvm line numbers refer to \strong{\code{\verb~|4cc6e20~}} (read with \code{\verb~|git show 4cc6e20:<path>~}), because that is the revision that scored 27.2 min / 11.8 GB.}
\li{\code{\verb~|refs/lean4~} (branch at \code{\verb~|611c117~}, v4.36 line) was used to check two claims about the official kernel.}
}

\p{All paths below are relative to \code{\verb~|refs/~}. Bare file names in §1 (\code{\verb~|machine.py~}, \code{\verb~|objects.py~}, \code{\verb~|parser.py~}, \code{\verb~|_eval.py~}, \code{\verb~|cli.py~}, \code{\verb~|environment.py~}, \code{\verb~|_inductive.py~}, \code{\verb~|_stack.py~}) live in \code{\verb~|rpylean/rpylean/~}; \code{\verb~|targetrpylean.py~} and \code{\verb~|justfile~} in \code{\verb~|rpylean/~}. Bare Java file names in §2 live in \code{\verb~|tenet-jvm/src/main/java/tenet/~}. "Commit \code{\verb~|abc1234~}" means a commit in the respective repository; quoted numbers are the authors' own measurements from commit messages (rpylean: Apple M4, ARM64 instruction counts) unless marked otherwise. Items I could not verify are marked \strong{\verb~|[~unverified\verb~|]~}; my own inferences are marked \strong{\verb~|[~inference\verb~|]~}.}

\subtree{
\title{0. Decision-relevant findings first}

\ol{
\li{\strong{rpylean is not a JIT-driven checker.} The translated binary is built with \code{\verb~|--opt=jit~} (\code{\verb~|rpylean/justfile:59~}), but the \em{only} \code{\verb~|JitDriver~} in the code base sits in \code{\verb~|rpylean/rpylean/_eval.py:1421~} and drives a call-by-need CEK machine that is entered solely when a \em{closed compound term is compared with a \code{\verb~|Bool~}/\code{\verb~|Nat~} scalar} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:11743-11761~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:8361-8389~}). Everything Mathlib spends time on — parsing, import, substitution, whnf, infer, def_eq — is RPython translated ahead-of-time to C. Measured effect of the JIT machine on library corpora: "init: ~0\% delta, std +1.3\%, cedar +1.6\%, cslib −0.1\%" (commit \code{\verb~|dd8949e~}).}
\li{\strong{The authors tried a tracing JIT on the kernel loops and removed it.} With \code{\verb~|JitDriver~}s on \code{\verb~|whnf~}, \code{\verb~|_def_eq_core~}, \code{\verb~|_instantiate~} and the app-spine loop (commits \code{\verb~|83555d3~}, \code{\verb~|78ca705~}, \code{\verb~|5479807~}): "init.ndjson runs 136.7s with --jit off vs 162.4s with the JIT on … Setting the compile threshold absurdly high reproduces the slow times, so the cost is not poor trace quality but the merge-point bookkeeping itself … ~15\% of wall time on a megamorphic tree-walk the tracer can't speed up" (commit \code{\verb~|1ba28a8~}); removed in \code{\verb~|c2be56a~}. \strong{Consequence for RLVM: do not put Truffle partial evaluation on the kernel's term-walking loops; reserve it for evaluation of closed Lean code.}}
\li{\strong{The single largest win was moving the working set out of the GC heap}: terms as 16-byte records in unmanaged \code{\verb~|u32~} arrays addressed by integer handles, hash-consed per declaration, with all caches as parallel integer arrays. init: 752 B → 184 B instructions, 3478 → 963 MB; std: 9.66 T → 348 B (28×) (commits \code{\verb~|0866ac8~}, \code{\verb~|2ec1abf~}). Stated motivation: GC tracing of retained reduction products was "~45\% of the run" on the std tail (commit \code{\verb~|d3e30e2~}). On the JVM the exact analogue is primitive \code{\verb~|int[]~}/\code{\verb~|long[]~} arrays (the collector never scans their contents).}
\li{\strong{rpylean's kernel is substitution-based (de Bruijn + locally-nameless FVars), not NbE.} Its speed comes from (a) hash-consing ⇒ handle identity ⇒ O(1) equality and array-indexed memo slots, (b) memoised, allocation-free multi-substitution, (c) aggressively \em{not doing work}: skipping proof arguments via per-constant Prop masks, comparing un-instantiated patterns against targets instead of instantiating (\code{\verb~|inst_eq~}), importing only what is needed from the parsed AST, warm caches across declarations. Closures were tried in the old object kernel and abandoned because fresh closure objects defeated identity-keyed caches (commit \code{\verb~|4c45e81~}); see §4.}
\li{\strong{Budget reference.} Arena: 96.3 s × 6e9 = \strong{5.78e11 instructions} for Mathlib, single-threaded, peak 4.4 GB. Own numbers on M4 at the pinned revision: init 28.7 G, std 50.2 G, cedar 68.8 G, cslib 115.5 G, navier-stokes-euler 193.6 G instructions (commit \code{\verb~|1f30f95~}). The last Mathlib figure recorded in git is 1285.5 G at \code{\verb~|ff75c0a~} (2026-11-21); the later commits cut NSE by 2.15× (415.6 G → 193.6 G), which extrapolates to ≈600 G \strong{\verb~|[~inference\verb~|]~}, consistent with the arena's 578 G. Mathlib has ~670 k declarations (commit \code{\verb~|a31ca02~}) and ~107 M expression nodes in the export (commit \code{\verb~|291ae24~}), so the bar is \strong{≈0.85 M instructions per declaration / ≈5.4 k instructions per exported expression node, everything included}.}
\li{\strong{tenet-jvm costs 9.8e12 instructions (17× rpylean) and 11.8 GB} for structural reasons that are all avoidable: a \code{\verb~|LinkedHashMap<String,Object>~} JSON tree per line, \code{\verb~|HashMap<Expr,Expr>~} caches with structural \code{\verb~|equals~}, non-interned \code{\verb~|Name~}s as \code{\verb~|HashMap~} keys, fresh FVars on every binder opening, closure-based generic \code{\verb~|replace~}, \code{\verb~|ArrayList~} spines, and a launcher (\code{\verb~|-XX:+UseParallelGC -XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75~}) that lets the heap grow to 12 GB on the 16 GB runner while all GC worker threads' instructions are billed. What is worth copying: the fail-closed verdict protocol, the large-stack checker thread, derive-then-compare for inductives, and its catalogue of Lean-version-dependent rules (§2.6).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1. rpylean}

\subtree{
\title{1.1 Architecture map}

\table{
\tr{\th{File (under \code{\verb~|rpylean/rpylean/~})}\th{Lines}\th{Role}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|parser.py~}}\td{2837}\td{NDJSON reader: SWAR chunk fast path + general cursor parser; refcount prescan; streaming hook per declaration}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|objects.py~}}\td{6391}\td{Parsed term language (\code{\verb~|W_Expr~}, \code{\verb~|Name~}, \code{\verb~|W_Level~}), declarations and their admission checks, interning tables, Nat ops, static Prop-mask / ctor-body analyses}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|machine.py~}}\td{12 879}\td{The kernel: \code{\verb~|TermStore~} (records, consing, substitution, import/export), \code{\verb~|Machine~} (whnf, infer, def_eq, check_value), raw \code{\verb~|IntMap~}/\code{\verb~|IntSet~}/\code{\verb~|U32Map~}/\code{\verb~|PairMap~}, warm-machine \code{\verb~|acquire~}/\code{\verb~|release~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_eval.py~}}\td{2031}\td{Call-by-need CEK machine over compiled \code{\verb~|CodeNode~}s for closed terms; the only JIT-traced loop}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_inductive.py~}}\td{1234}\td{Regenerates recursors of an inductive block (mutual + nested) for comparison}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|environment.py~}}\td{612}\td{\code{\verb~|Environment~} (name → decl), \code{\verb~|TypeChecker~} (per-declaration limits, ordering/safety rules), \code{\verb~|type_check_one~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|cli.py~}}\td{1139}\td{\code{\verb~|check~} command, streaming checker, prescan orchestration, exit codes}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_stack.py~}}\td{120}\td{Re-exec with a larger \code{\verb~|RLIMIT_STACK~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|targetrpylean.py~} (repo root)}\td{94}\td{Translation target; patches the GC nursery floor}}
}

\p{Data flow for \code{\verb~|./rpylean-c check FILE~} (\code{\verb~|cli.py:532-587~}):}

\pre{\verb~|
open FILE unbuffered ──► pass 1: prescan_refcounts (raw bytes → RefCountTable u32[exprIdx])   parser.py:2827, cli.py:491
        seek(0)      ──► pass 2: _consume_stream: 256 KiB chunks, SWAR fast path per line       parser.py:2722-2816
                              │ names/levels/exprs → GC objects (W_Expr AST), pool slot freed when refcount hits 0
                              ▼ each declaration line → EnvironmentBuilder.register_declaration → hook.on_declaration
                         _StreamingChecker.on_declaration (cli.py:274) → Environment.type_check_one (environment.py:406)
                              │ TypeChecker(env, decl) → acquire(warm Machine)                  machine.py:12809
                              ▼ decl.w_kind.type_check → Machine.check_value(type, value, prop) machine.py:12690
                         on success: decl.w_kind.drop_checked_value()  (theorem/opaque bodies freed) cli.py:363
exit 1 if any failure else 0 (cli.py:184)
~}

\p{Single-threaded; declarations are checked strictly in file order, interleaved with parsing. No decline exit code exists: deep recursion, per-declaration limits and malformed lines are all rejections (exit 1); an uncaught RPython exception aborts the process.}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.2 Two term representations}

\p{\strong{(A) Parsed AST — GC objects, immutable, persistent} (\code{\verb~|objects.py~}). Used only as the \em{source} from which the kernel store imports.}

\ul{
\li{\p{\code{\verb~|W_Expr~} base: two words, \code{\verb~|_packed~} and \code{\verb~|_cache~} (\code{\verb~|objects.py:2808-2850~}).}
\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|_packed~}: bits 0-31 content hash; bit 32 \code{\verb~|has_fvar~}; bits 33-61 \code{\verb~|loose_bvar_range~}; bit 62 \code{\verb~|has_level_param~}. Computed in each constructor (\code{\verb~|W_App.__init__~}, \code{\verb~|objects.py:4314-4324~}).}
\li{\code{\verb~|_cache~}: \code{\verb~|(generation << 32) | handle~} — an \em{intrusive, generation-stamped import memo} (see §1.4).}
}}
\li{\code{\verb~|W_App{fn,arg}~}, \code{\verb~|W_Lambda/W_ForAll{binder,body}~} with \code{\verb~|Binder{name,type,_pos_style,_fvar}~}, \code{\verb~|W_Let{name,type,value,body}~}, \code{\verb~|W_Proj{struct_name,field_index,struct_expr}~}, \code{\verb~|W_Const{name,levels,_canonical}~}, \code{\verb~|W_Sort{level}~}, \code{\verb~|W_BVar{id}~}, \code{\verb~|W_FVar{id,binder,_uid}~}, \code{\verb~|W_LitNat{val: rbigint}~}, \code{\verb~|W_LitStr{val}~}.}
\li{Interning policy (\code{\verb~|objects.py:1024-1047~}): \code{\verb~|Name~}s globally hash-consed in append-only open-addressed tables storing \code{\verb~|(hash31 << 32) | (entryIdx+1)~} in a pointer-free int list (\code{\verb~|objects.py:961-1100~}) ⇒ name equality is pointer identity; levels hash-consed in per-kind dicts; \code{\verb~|W_Const~} in a fixed 65 536-slot direct-mapped cache (\code{\verb~|_CONST_CACHE~}); \code{\verb~|W_BVar~}/small \code{\verb~|W_LitNat~} in 1024-entry arrays; \code{\verb~|W_Sort~}, \code{\verb~|W_LitStr~} interned. \strong{\code{\verb~|W_App~}/\code{\verb~|W_Proj~}/\code{\verb~|W_Let~}/binders are deliberately \em{not} globally interned} — "lean4export already DAG-shares parsed terms by \code{\verb~|ie~} index and \code{\verb~|TermStore~} hash-conses them per declaration; keeping strong refs in global dicts pinned dead theorem proofs across Mathlib".}
\li{Per-\code{\verb~|Name~} inline cache of the declaration lookup: \code{\verb~|get_decl~} is two field reads (\code{\verb~|name._decl_dict is declarations → name._decl_cached~}, \code{\verb~|objects.py:47-64~}); −4.8\% instructions on a grind workload (commit \code{\verb~|7073bce~}).}
\li{Levels: parsed verbatim (no simplification at parse, commit \code{\verb~|eed3160~}); \code{\verb~|eq~} = identity, else syntactic equality of cached normal forms, else \code{\verb~|leq~} both ways (\code{\verb~|objects.py:2196-2208~}); \code{\verb~|normalize()~} cached on the level object. Constant and sort leaves are canonicalised to normal-form levels on import so \code{\verb~|C.{max u v}~} and \code{\verb~|C.{max v u}~} become the same leaf (\code{\verb~|machine.py:517-552~}; commit \code{\verb~|c147f1d~}: one declaration 22 s / 4.87 M def_eq calls → 1.2 s / 200 calls).}
}

\p{\strong{(B) Kernel store — \code{\verb~|TermStore~}, unmanaged memory, per declaration (warm-reused)} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:83-152~}, \code{\verb~|1114-1272~}).}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Handle} = tagged int. bit 0 set ⇒ leaf with index \code{\verb~|h >> 1~}; bit 0 clear and ≠ 0 ⇒ record with index \code{\verb~|(h >> 1) − 1~}; \code{\verb~|0~} = invalid/empty marker of every table.}
\li{\p{\strong{Record} = 4 × \code{\verb~|u32~} (16 bytes) in \code{\verb~|recs~}:}
\ul{
\li{word 0: \code{\verb~|(meta << 3) | kind~}, \code{\verb~|meta = (loose_bvar_range << 1) | has_fvar~}. Hence \code{\verb~|word0 < 16 ⇔ no loose bvars~} — a one-compare "nothing to substitute here" test used everywhere (\code{\verb~|machine.py:2500~}).}
\li{word 1 \code{\verb~|a~}, word 2 \code{\verb~|b~}: child handles. \code{\verb~|APP(fn,arg)~}, \code{\verb~|LAMBDA/FORALL(binderType, body)~}, \code{\verb~|PROJ(struct, (nameId << 10) | fieldIdx)~}, \code{\verb~|LET(type, PAIR(value, body))~}, \code{\verb~|PAIR~}.}
\li{word 3: \code{\verb~|(sizeEnc:8 << 24) | info:24~}. \code{\verb~|sizeEnc~} = saturating tree size (255 = "heavy", ≥ 256 nodes), computed on cons as \code{\verb~|ea + eb + 2~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:1632-1639~}); \code{\verb~|info~} = index into a GC side list holding the \code{\verb~|Binder~} (name, style — not part of identity) or the projection/let \code{\verb~|Name~}.}
}}
\li{\strong{Identity}: \code{\verb~|(kind, a, b)~}. Binders are consed on (type, body) only ⇒ alpha-equal binders share a record. Projection identity includes the structure name (bug fixed in \code{\verb~|2ec1abf~}: \code{\verb~|PProd.0 x~} and \code{\verb~|LE.0 x~} had shared a record).}
\li{\strong{Memo slots}: 6 × \code{\verb~|u32~} per record in \code{\verb~|memos~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:145-158~}): \code{\verb~|M_WHNF_CORE~}, \code{\verb~|M_WHNF~}, \code{\verb~|M_INFER~}, \code{\verb~|M_CHECKED_GEN~}, \code{\verb~|M_WHNF_CORE_CHEAP~} (also holds the one-step delta unfold of a delta-headed app, tagged with bit 31), \code{\verb~|M_EQV~} (union-find parent). 0 = unknown. Plus one \code{\verb~|i64~} \code{\verb~|call_slot~} per record (scratch memo of the substitution in progress, §1.5).}
\li{\p{\strong{Consing tables} (open addressing, linear probing, load ≤ 50\%, single multiply-xorshift hash \code{\verb~|_spread~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:329-336~}):}
\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|app_table~}: one \code{\verb~|i64~} per slot = \code{\verb~|(fn:21 | arg:21 | recIdx+1:21)~}. A hit needs \strong{one probe of one array and no load from \code{\verb~|recs~}} (\code{\verb~|cons_app~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:1589-1605~}). When any handle ≥ 2²¹ the table is promoted to a 16-byte \code{\verb~|(key64, handle)~} layout (\code{\verb~|_promote_apps_to_wide~}).}
\li{\code{\verb~|table~} for the other kinds: \code{\verb~|(kind:3 | a:20 | b:20 | recIdx+1:20)~}, promoted above 2²⁰.}
}
\pre{\verb~|
cons_app(fn, arg):                                   # machine.py:1589-1647
  if (fn | arg) >= 2^21: return cons_app_wide(fn, arg)
  pair = (fn << 21) | arg
  i = spread(pair) & mask                            # spread(k): x = (k ^ k>>>30) * 0xbf58476d1ce4e5b9; x ^= x>>>27
  loop:
    e = app_table[i]
    if (e >> 21) == pair: return (e & (2^21-1)) << 1  # hit: handle = (recIdx+1) << 1, no load from recs
    if e == 0: break
    i = (i + 1) & mask
  # miss (out of line): append record
  meta = max(looseRange(fn), looseRange(arg)) << 1 | (hasFVar(fn) | hasFVar(arg))
  size = min(255, sizeEnc(fn) + sizeEnc(arg) + 2)     # leaves count 0
  recs[4*n .. 4*n+3] = [(meta << 3) | APP, fn, arg, size << 24];  n += 1
  if ++napps * 2 > tableSize: rehash_apps() else app_table[i] = (pair << 21) | n
  return n << 1
~}}
\li{\strong{Leaves} (constants, sorts, bvars, fvars, literals) stay GC objects in a list \code{\verb~|leaves[j]~}, canonicalised on entry (\code{\verb~|leaf_for~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:2144-2219~}: bvars by index, fvars by identity, the rest by content after level normalisation). Parallel unmanaged per-leaf arrays: \code{\verb~|leaf_meta~}, \code{\verb~|leaf_whnf~}, \code{\verb~|leaf_infer~}, \code{\verb~|leaf_checked~}, \code{\verb~|leaf_delta~} (imported unfolded value), \code{\verb~|leaf_delta_body~} (stripped body + arity, or a tagged fast-path encoding), \code{\verb~|leaf_eqv~}, \code{\verb~|leaf_head_kind~} (classification flags \code{\verb~|_LF_RECURSOR | _LF_QUOT_LIFT | _LF_DELTA | _LF_CTOR | _LF_NAT_BINOP | _LF_ITE | _LF_SHORT_BOOL | _LF_NAT_SUCC | _LF_NAT_ZERO~} + the reducibility hint in the high 16 bits), \code{\verb~|leaf_prop_mask~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:1166-1190~}, flags at \code{\verb~|427-439~}). A head constant is classified once per store; afterwards "is this head a recursor / unfoldable / a ctor / a native Nat op, and what is its height" is one array load.}
\li{\strong{Spine buffer}: \code{\verb~|_spine_buf~} (\code{\verb~|u32[]~}) with a stack discipline — \code{\verb~|mark = top; head = unapp_push(h); n = top − mark; …; unapp_pop(mark)~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:2335-2358~}). Application arguments are never materialised as lists; beta, iota, delta, infer and def_eq all read arguments from this buffer.}
\li{Size per record of capacity ≈ 16 (recs) + 24 (memos) + 8 (call_slot) + 16 (app_table at 2 slots/record) ≈ 64 bytes; no per-node object header, nothing traced by the GC.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.3 Export parsing}

\ul{
\li{\p{Two passes over the file when it is seekable (\code{\verb~|cli.py:546-557~}):}
\ol{
\li{\strong{Prescan} (\code{\verb~|_prescan_chunk_fast~}, \code{\verb~|parser.py:1353-1548~}): raw-byte scan that, per expression index, counts how many later lines reference it, into a pre-sized unmanaged \code{\verb~|u32~} \code{\verb~|RefCountTable~} (size hint \code{\verb~|fileSize/50~}). Name and level lines are skipped with a SWAR newline search (\code{\verb~|_find_nl~}, \code{\verb~|parser.py:604-615~}).}
\li{\strong{Parse}: every reference goes through \code{\verb~|ref_expr~}, which decrements the count and nulls the pool slot at zero (\code{\verb~|parser.py:256-277~}). Together with dropping theorem/opaque bodies after their check this bounds the live AST to "declarations still in play": cslib 14.8 → 8.6 GB and 1.5× faster; "mathlib live heap collapses from ~8 GB to ~1.5 GB as it checks"; "~68\% of cslib's distinct expressions are reachable only from theorem values" (commit \code{\verb~|1f6d220~}).}
}}
\li{I/O: unbuffered \code{\verb~|read(262144)~}; chunks are parsed \strong{in place}; only the line straddling a chunk boundary is concatenated (\code{\verb~|parser.py:2727-2816~}). Before this, \code{\verb~|memmove~} was "59\% of all L1D store misses"; fixing it cut footprint 48-57\% and init wall time 10.8\% (commit \code{\verb~|291ae24~}).}
\li{Fast path = word-at-a-time (SWAR) matching of the \em{canonical lean4export key order} with unaligned 64/32/16-bit loads compared against compile-time packed literals (\code{\verb~|parser.py:427-522~}): \code{\verb~|{"app":{"arg":A,"fn":F},"ie":E}~} ("~73\% of all lines", \code{\verb~|parser.py:1381~}), \code{\verb~|{"ie":E,"lam":{"binderInfo":…,"body":B,"name":N,"type":T}}~}, \code{\verb~|{"forallE":{…},"ie":E}~}; a second tier (\code{\verb~|_compact_rare~}) handles const/sort/bvar/letE/proj/natVal/strVal/names/levels/def/thm/opaque; anything else (different key order, whitespace) falls back to a general cursor parser (\code{\verb~|parse_cursor_general~}, \code{\verb~|parser.py:1570~}). No JSON tree, no per-line object except the AST node itself. Gain of the SWAR rewrite: −5.1…−6.0\% of \em{total} instructions on init/std/cedar/cslib, −3.0\% on NSE (commit \code{\verb~|437cefa~}).}
\li{No mmap, no parallel parsing, no binary cache format. Parse share of the total is not reported anywhere \strong{\verb~|[~unverified\verb~|]~}; the −5…6\% figure above is a lower bound on what it was before the rewrite.}
\li{Robustness rules worth copying: metadata line validated (\code{\verb~|EXPORT_VERSION = "3.1.0"~}, a missing version is tolerated, \code{\verb~|parser.py:381-395~}); a malformed line is an \code{\verb~|ExportError~} ⇒ rejection, never a crash (commits \code{\verb~|f9ccf0e~}, \code{\verb~|3041b64~}); UTF-16 surrogate pairs in \code{\verb~|\u~} escapes are combined and string literals are expanded per Unicode scalar, not per byte (commit \code{\verb~|c7a68d7~}, arena \code{\verb~|bugs/str-lit-utf8*~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.4 Import: AST → store, fused with level and argument substitution}

\p{This is the part with no counterpart in the Rust checkers and worth understanding precisely.}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|import_term(e)~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:5989-6164~}): memoised by \code{\verb~|e._cache == (store_gen << 32) | handle~}; iterative along application spines (explicit \code{\verb~|_import_spine~} stack), recursive elsewhere with a stack check every 32 frames.}
\li{\code{\verb~|import_const_term(const, decl, target)~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:6555-6587~}): imports \code{\verb~|target~} (a declaration's type, value or recursor-rule RHS) \strong{with \code{\verb~|decl.levels := const.levels~} substituted during the walk}, never building an instantiated AST. Sub-terms without level params (\code{\verb~|has_level_param~} bit) reuse the plain memo. The memo for the level-instantiated walk uses a \em{different generation number} per (params, levels) pair, obtained from a 512-slot direct-mapped table (\code{\verb~|_level_cache_gen~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:6489-6553~}), so one \code{\verb~|_cache~} word per AST node serves "this node under this level instantiation in this store epoch". Identity instantiations (\code{\verb~|C.{u}~} inside a declaration polymorphic in \code{\verb~|u~}) short-circuit to the plain import.}
\li{\strong{Never import what beta will discard} (commit \code{\verb~|90bc723~}, NSE −3.4\%): for an applied definition, the leading lambdas of the value are peeled \em{on the AST} and only the body is imported; \code{\verb~|leaf_delta_body[j] = (arity << 32) | bodyHandle~}. Same for recursor rules (\code{\verb~|_rule_rhs_stripped~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:9386~}).}
\li{\strong{First-use fusion} (commit \code{\verb~|e974694~}; \code{\verb~|_try_unfold_first_use~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:8133-8270~}): the first time a definition is unfolded in a store, level substitution \em{and} argument substitution are done in one walk of the AST (\code{\verb~|import_const_subst_buf~}), producing the beta-reduct directly; only the second unfold imports the stripped body into the store ("single-use definitions are ~40-55\% of \code{\verb~|_delta_body~} records").}
\li{\strong{Delta fast paths by body shape} (commit \code{\verb~|769f42b~}; \code{\verb~|_unfold_fast~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:8058-8130~}): if the value is \code{\verb~|λ x₁…xₘ. BVar b~} (argument picker: \code{\verb~|outParam~}, \code{\verb~|inferInstance~}, \code{\verb~|id~}-likes) or \code{\verb~|λ x₁…xₘ. Proj(S, i, BVar b)~} (structure/class parent projections), the unfold is computed from the spine without any import or instantiate.}
\li{Analogous AST-direct paths exist for inference of constant applications on first use (\code{\verb~|_infer_app_const_ast_buf~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:10898~}; "single-use constants are ~78\% of \code{\verb~|_infer_leaf~} records", \code{\verb~|machine.py:463-468~}) and for projection field types (\code{\verb~|W_Inductive.init_proj_cache~}, \code{\verb~|objects.py:5900-5925~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.5 Substitution engine}

\p{All of \code{\verb~|instantiate~}, \code{\verb~|instantiate_multi*~}, \code{\verb~|shift~}, \code{\verb~|bind_fvar(s)~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:2451-5950~}) follow one scheme:}

\pre{\verb~|
instantiate(h, sub, depth):
  if looseRange(h) <= depth: return h                      # one load + compare
  if leaf(h): bvar hit → sub (shifted by depth unless sub closed); else bvar(id-1)
  r = persistentMemo[(h, sub, depth)]  (packed 25|25|13 bits into one i64 key; capped table) ; if r: return r
  epoch = ++callEpoch
  r = walk(h)        # recursive; per record ri visited:
                     #   if callSlot[ri] >> 32 == (epoch << 8 | depth): return low 32 bits   ← O(1) one-shot memo
                     #   rebuild children; if unchanged return h itself (no cons)
                     #   left spines of APP are unrolled iteratively onto _subst_stack
                     #   callSlot[ri] = ((epoch << 8 | depth) << 32) | result
  persistentMemo[(h, sub, depth)] = r
~}

\ul{
\li{The \strong{one-shot memo} (\code{\verb~|call_slot~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:1253-1255~}, \code{\verb~|2502-2505~}, \code{\verb~|2659~}) makes substitution linear in the DAG with no hashing: one \code{\verb~|i64~} array indexed by record, validated by a per-call epoch. A record seen at a second depth within one call falls back to a small \code{\verb~|IntMap~} (\code{\verb~|_call_memo~}). Replacing per-call \code{\verb~|IntMap~} hashing by this: "−10\% to −15\% cycles & instructions across the board" (commit \code{\verb~|53c4861~}, together with 32-bit arrays and the spine buffer).}
\li{\strong{Multi-substitution} takes its substitutes directly from a slice of the spine buffer (\code{\verb~|instantiate_multi_buf(h, start, count)~}), so an n-ary beta/iota/delta step is one walk with zero list allocation; specialised variants exist for depth 0 and for "all substitutes closed" (no shifting) (\code{\verb~|machine.py:3891-3920~}; commits \code{\verb~|ff75c0a~}, \code{\verb~|7e11d57~}).}
\li{The persistent memos (\code{\verb~|_inst_memo~}, \code{\verb~|_shift_memo~}, \code{\verb~|_bind_memo~}, \code{\verb~|_multi_memo~}) are capped (\code{\verb~|_MEMO_LIMIT = 1 << 18~} slots, \code{\verb~|machine.py:503-506~}) and wiped when full: "a substitution memo only pays for itself while a lookup is cheaper than redoing the work, which stops being true once the table has outgrown the caches" (commit \code{\verb~|19c0af8~}).}
\li{\strong{Telescopes are opened at once} (commit \code{\verb~|6087a53~}): a k-binder lambda is instantiated with k fvars in one multi-substitution and re-abstracted in one \code{\verb~|bind_fvars~} pass; before, "a k-binder lambda cost k walks of each"; the abstraction memo of the slowest Mathlib declaration shrank 53 M → 5 M entries.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.6 Reduction}

\p{\code{\verb~|whnf_core(h, cheap_proj)~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:7728-7911~}) — beta, zeta, proj-of-ctor, iota, \code{\verb~|Quot.lift~}; never delta. Memo slot per mode; a result known in \code{\verb~|M_WHNF~} also answers \code{\verb~|whnf_core~}. One step (\code{\verb~|_whnf_core_step~}):}

\ul{
\li{\p{\code{\verb~|APP~}: walk to the head without materialising the spine.}
\ul{
\li{head is a record \code{\verb~|LAMBDA~} → push spine, \strong{multi-arg beta} (\code{\verb~|_beta_spine_buf~}: strip up to n lambdas, one multi-instantiate, re-apply leftovers).}
\li{head is a leaf: one flag load; unless \code{\verb~|_LF_RECURSOR~}/\code{\verb~|_LF_QUOT_LIFT~}, \strong{stuck in O(1)}.}
\li{recursor → \code{\verb~|_try_iota_spine~} (below); \code{\verb~|Quot.lift~} with ≥ 6 args → whnf the 6th, must be \code{\verb~|Quot.mk~} with 3 args → \code{\verb~|f a extra…~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:9146-9164~}).}
\li{head is \code{\verb~|PROJ~}/\code{\verb~|LET~} → reduce head, re-apply (beta directly if it became a lambda).}
}}
\li{\code{\verb~|LET~} → instantiate body with value. \code{\verb~|PROJ~} → \code{\verb~|try_proj~}.}
}

\p{\code{\verb~|whnf(h)~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:7913-7943~}): \code{\verb~|loop { h = whnf_core(h); if APP and try_reduce_nat(h) → continue; u = try_unfold_head(h); if u == 0 break; h = u }~}, memoised in \code{\verb~|M_WHNF~} / \code{\verb~|leaf_whnf~}. One delta layer per iteration; the one-step unfold of an app is itself memoised (commit \code{\verb~|cb628e6~}).}

\p{\strong{Iota} (\code{\verb~|_try_iota_spine~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:9166-9384~}):}

\ol{
\li{\code{\verb~|Nat.rec~} on a literal major: done in one step without constructing \code{\verb~|Nat.succ~} (builds \code{\verb~|succ_case pred (Nat.rec … pred)~} with \code{\verb~|pred~} a literal).}
\li{\code{\verb~|major = whnf(major)~}; if the recursor is K-like, \code{\verb~|_to_cnstr_when_k~} (infer + whnf the major's type, build the nullary-field ctor applied to the type's params, require \code{\verb~|def_eq(type, infer(ctor))~}; \code{\verb~|machine.py:9404-9446~}).}
\li{literal major → expose one constructor; otherwise try structure-eta of a stuck major (\code{\verb~|_to_cnstr_when_structure~}, see §1.12 for a deviation).}
\li{head must be a ctor; rule looked up by ctor name (\code{\verb~|rec.rule_for_ctor~}).}
\li{\strong{Rule fast paths} (commits \code{\verb~|769f42b~}, \code{\verb~|b486214~}): \code{\verb~|W_RecRule.simple_minor~} (\code{\verb~|objects.py:4498-4585~}) recognises, once per rule, the standard shape \code{\verb~|λ params motives minors fields ⇒ minor_i fields (rec … field_r)…~} and records the minor index and the list of recursive field positions. Then iota is computed straight from the spine: pick the minor, push fields and the IH applications \code{\verb~|rec_prefix field_r~} (re-using the \code{\verb~|rec params motives minors~} prefix record of the redex), and beta in one step — the rule RHS is never imported or instantiated. Otherwise the stripped RHS is imported once per (recursor leaf, ctor leaf) and applied by one multi-instantiate.}
}

\p{\strong{Projection} (\code{\verb~|try_proj~} / \code{\verb~|_try_proj_fused~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:8997-9144~}; commits \code{\verb~|cdc2edb~}, \code{\verb~|70a43a3~}, \code{\verb~|6d4475f~}): nested projections are peeled onto an index stack; when the struct reduces to an application of a \em{definition whose body is a constructor application} (statically analysed once: \code{\verb~|W_Definition.init_ctor_body~} → \code{\verb~|_CtorBody{m, num_params, let_vals, args, delegate_const}~}, \code{\verb~|objects.py:5114-5338~}, including wrappers delegating to another such definition up to depth 6), \strong{only the projected field is imported and instantiated}, with only the arguments it mentions; fields that are a bare \code{\verb~|BVar~} are read from the spine. This is the type-class-instance fast path (\code{\verb~|instFoo.toBar.op~} without materialising the whole instance).}

\p{\strong{Nat literals} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:8361-8505~}, ops in \code{\verb~|objects.py:3500-3579~}): \code{\verb~|add sub mul pow gcd mod div beq ble land lor xor shiftLeft shiftRight~} on \code{\verb~|rbigint~}; \code{\verb~|pow~}/\code{\verb~|shiftLeft~} decline when the exponent/shift exceeds 2²⁴. \code{\verb~|try_reduce_nat~} whnf's both arguments (so it evaluates) and is therefore called only from the evaluating \code{\verb~|whnf~} loop; lazy delta uses \code{\verb~|try_reduce_nat_cheap~} (arguments must already be syntactic numerals) and only on fvar-free terms (commit \code{\verb~|2c7d435~} explains the blow-up otherwise). Arguments that are closed non-literals go to the CEK machine first (\code{\verb~|_whnf_nat_arg~}).}

\p{\strong{String literals}: expanded lazily to \code{\verb~|String.ofList [Char.ofNat n, …]~} (per code point) only when projected, matched by a recursor, or as the last resort of def_eq (\code{\verb~|objects.py:3156-3165~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:12369-12380~}).}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.7 Definitional equality — exact order}

\p{\code{\verb~|def_eq(h1, h2)~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:11591-11622~}):}

\pre{\verb~|
1. h1 == h2                                             → true      (hash-consing: syntactic equality)
2. eqvCount > 0 and find(h1) == find(h2)                → true      (union-find in M_EQV / leaf_eqv, path compression)
3. symmetric pair key in _neq                           → false     (negative cache: IntSet, 8 B/slot, capped at 4M slots)
4. both APP and eqvCount > 0: _spine_cheap_eq           → union; true
      lockstep walk down both spines; every arg pair identical or in the same UF class,
      heads identical or same class; no recursion, no reduction             (machine.py:11682-11701)
5. r = _def_eq_uncached(h1, h2);  r ? union(h1,h2) : _neq.add(key)
~}

\p{\code{\verb~|_def_eq_uncached~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:11740-11813~}):}

\pre{\verb~|
a. if one side is a Bool/Nat scalar leaf and the other a closed compound term (not a Nat.succ chain):
       v = eval_closed_scalar(other); if v == scalar → true; else continue with v     (§1.10)
b. h1 = whnf_core(h1, cheap_proj=true); h2 likewise; identical → true
c. proof irrelevance (before any delta): t1 = infer(h1); s1 = infer(t1) (whnf only if not literally Prop);
       if Prop: same for h2; if def_eq(t1, t2) → true          (falls through on failure)
d. Nat offset: both literals → compare; both Nat.zero → true; peel matching Nat.succ/literal layers in a loop
e. if one side is the leaf Bool.true: whnf(other) == Bool.true → true
f. status = lazy_delta(h1, h2)  → true, or continue with the advanced forms; identical → true
g. _def_eq_proj_lazy: two projections (bare or applied heads) with the same (struct name, index):
       bounded comparison of the structs (shared budget of 8 unfold steps, recursion depth 3), guarded by _failed
h. n1 = whnf_core(h1) (full, projections evaluated), n2 likewise; if either changed → def_eq(n1, n2)
i. _def_eq_core:
     leaves: sorts → level eq; consts → same name and level-wise eq; distinct literals/fvars → fall through
     APP/APP → _def_eq_app;  binders of same kind → _def_eq_binders;  PROJ/PROJ same field → def_eq(structs)
     eta (lambda vs non-lambda whose whnf'd type is a Pi) in both directions
     structure eta in both directions (ctor app with exactly params+fields args; def_eq of the types; field-wise def_eq with projections)
     unit-like (type is a non-recursive, index-free structure whose ctor has 0 fields; def_eq of the types)
     Nat literal → one constructor step; String literal → String.ofList expansion
~}

\p{\strong{Lazy delta} (\code{\verb~|_try_lazy_delta~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:12059-12285~}), per iteration (cap 100 000):}

\pre{\verb~|
1. identical → true
2. peel Nat offsets (as in d); if peeled, cheap whnf_core both
3. if neither side has fvars: try_reduce_nat_cheap on either APP → continue
4. d1/d2 = head has _LF_DELTA.  neither → return UNDEF(h1,h2)
5. exactly one unfoldable: unfold it (native Nat op first if closed); if the *other* head is a PROJ,
   try _def_eq_proj_lazy on the cheap-whnf'd result before full whnf_core
6. both unfoldable:
   a. exactly one is @[reducible]/abbrev → unfold that one
   b. exactly one is a fully applied ite/dite whose Decidable instance is closed → unfold that one   ← not in Lean
   c. same constant (name equal, levels eq) with a *regular* hint: unless it is Bool.and/or with a
      reducible first argument (short-circuit, not in Lean), compare arguments pairwise left to right —
      skipping positions in the head's Prop mask — guarded by the _failed pair cache; all equal → true
   d. exactly one head is a native Nat binop → unfold the *other* side first                         ← not in Lean
   e. greater height unfolds; equal heights → unfold both, cheap whnf_core, identical or proj-lazy → true
~}

\p{Deliberate differences from the official kernel that matter for performance:}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Prop-argument masks} (\code{\verb~|_prop_mask_for~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:7585-7665~}; static analysis \code{\verb~|W_Declaration.init_prop_mask~}, \code{\verb~|objects.py:4843-4967~}). For a head constant, a 62-bit mask of argument positions whose domain is a proposition. In \code{\verb~|_def_eq_app~}, lazy delta's same-head comparison and \code{\verb~|_proj_lazy_eq~}, once all earlier arguments agreed, an unequal argument pair at a masked position is \strong{skipped} (proof irrelevance without inferring anything). Computed from the declared type without the store for "~99.7\% of constant heads": binder domain is \code{\verb~|∀…, Sort l~} (never a proof position); or \code{\verb~|BVar~} applied to as many args as an earlier binder's \code{\verb~|∀…, Sort l~} arity (position is Prop iff \code{\verb~|l~} is zero); or \code{\verb~|C args~} with \code{\verb~|C : ∀ (m args), Sort l~} fully applied (Prop iff the instantiated \code{\verb~|l~} normalises to zero). Level-dependent cases get a small "plan" evaluated per level instantiation; the trailing result type must provably not unfold to further Prop-domain Pis; anything else falls back to a dynamic computation with fvars and \code{\verb~|infer~}. Active only while a declaration is being checked. \strong{Effect: NSE −24.4\% instructions (339.3 → 256.7 G), proof-irrelevance fallbacks −99.8\% (1.41 M → 3.3 K), beta reductions −54.4\%} (commit \code{\verb~|c87c5b4~}).}
\li{\strong{Negative cache \code{\verb~|_neq~} for every def_eq} (the reference kernel caches only the same-head failure). Sound because a handle pair determines the answer within a store (fvars are canonical, §1.8).}
\li{\strong{Spine congruence pre-pass} (step 4; "modeled on nanobruijn's spec_app_congruence", −1.4\% instructions and −16\% peak memory on init, commit \code{\verb~|b249a47~}).}
\li{\strong{Lazy projection equality} and \strong{closed-ite / Bool short-circuit / Nat-binop ordering} heuristics (steps g, 6b-6d).}
\li{Stats from the earlier object kernel on init, still indicative of where def_eq calls end: "83\% of the 129M def_eq calls resolve by pointer identity, the eqv union-find hits 86\% of the calls that get past it"; the failed-pair cache had only 952 hits in 286 k probes but each "is insurance against re-exploring a pathologically expensive same-head args refutation" (commit \code{\verb~|4746484~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.8 Type inference}

\p{\code{\verb~|infer(h, check)~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:9570-9607~}), two modes as in Lean:}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|check = false~} (everything reached from inside def_eq/whnf): only computes; memo in \code{\verb~|M_INFER~} / \code{\verb~|leaf_infer~}. An application's type is obtained by walking the head type's Pi telescope \strong{without instantiating}, keeping a count \code{\verb~|plen~} of pending arguments and substituting them all at once only when a non-Pi is hit or at the end (\code{\verb~|_infer_app_only_buf~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:11134-11172~}).}
\li{\code{\verb~|check = true~} (only the declaration's own type and value): additionally argument-type-vs-domain def_eq, binder domains are sorts, let values, universe params declared, and the reference rules (declared earlier, not less safe). The memo is the same \code{\verb~|M_INFER~} slot, validated by \code{\verb~|M_CHECKED_GEN >= machine.check_gen~} — one generation counter instead of a second cache.}
}

\p{Tricks:}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Canonical free variables} (\code{\verb~|fvar_for_domain~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:9505-9534~}): opening binder record \code{\verb~|h~} whose instantiated domain is \code{\verb~|d~} always yields the same fvar leaf, via the map \code{\verb~|(h, d) → fvar~}. Re-opening a shared lambda therefore produces the \em{same} instantiated body handle, so every memo (infer, whnf, def_eq) hits. The fvar's type lives in \code{\verb~|leaf_infer~}. (For top-level telescopes a second map \code{\verb~|(position, domain) → fvar~} gives consecutive declarations with a common \code{\verb~|variable~} prefix the same fvars, \code{\verb~|_top_fvar~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:9546~}.)}
\li{\p{\strong{\code{\verb~|inst_eq~}: compare instead of instantiate} (\code{\verb~|inst_eq_buf~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:3120-3125~}; commits \code{\verb~|d749f43~}, \code{\verb~|489f178~}). When checking argument \em{i} of \code{\verb~|f a₁…aₙ~}, the domain is \code{\verb~|Aᵢ[a₁…aᵢ₋₁]~}. Instead of building it, the inferred argument type (a handle) is compared structurally against the \em{pattern} \code{\verb~|Aᵢ~} + the pending arguments in the spine buffer (budget 512 steps). Only on mismatch is the domain instantiated and \code{\verb~|def_eq~} called.}
\pre{\verb~|
inst_eq(pat, args[0..n), target, depth = 0, budget = 512) -> bool      # "instantiate(pat, args) == target ?" without consing
  if looseRange(pat) <= depth: return pat == target                     # closed part: handle identity
  if leaf(pat):  # a loose bvar
      k = bvarIndex(pat) - depth                                        # k >= 0 here
      if k < n:  return args[k] == target and (depth == 0 or looseRange(args[k]) == 0)   # no shifting ⇒ else give up
      return target == bvar(bvarIndex(pat) - n)
  if --budget < 0 or leaf(target) or kind(target) != kind(pat): return false
  APP:           iterate down both spines: inst_eq(arg_p, arg_t) for each, then heads
  LAMBDA/FORALL: inst_eq(type_p, type_t, depth) and inst_eq(body_p, body_t, depth + 1)
  PROJ:          same (name, index) and inst_eq(struct_p, struct_t)
# false means "unknown": the caller instantiates and runs the full def_eq
~}
\p{The same test against an \em{expected type} lets \code{\verb~|_infer_app~} return the expected handle without instantiating the result type (\code{\verb~|infer_expected~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:9609~}), and a pattern-vs-pattern variant (\code{\verb~|inst_eq_inst_buf~}) handles nested applications; there is even an AST-direct variant that never imports the constant's type (\code{\verb~|_ast_inst_eq~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:3137~}).}}
\li{\strong{Joint telescope check} (\code{\verb~|_check_value_joint_ast~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:12600-12688~}; commit \code{\verb~|8d7da87~}: init −4.7\%, cslib −5.9\%, NSE −7.3\% instructions): for \code{\verb~|def/theorem c : ∀ xs, T := λ xs, v~} with identical leading domains, each domain is checked once, the fvars are shared between type and value, and \code{\verb~|v~} is inferred with \code{\verb~|T~} as expected type; then \code{\verb~|def_eq(T, typeof v)~}.}
\li{\strong{Inference without substitution for heavy terms} (\code{\verb~|_infer_open*~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:10249-10450~}; commit \code{\verb~|1f0405e~}): once a declaration's store exceeds 2¹⁷ records, a term of ≥ 256 nodes under binders is inferred against a \em{context} (list of fvars / let values, plus a consed "chain" handle used as cache key) and sub-terms are materialised only when light or when a type comes to depend on them. \code{\verb~|perf/app-lam~}: 32 B → 0.43 B instructions, 10 GB → 86 MB. \strong{Important counter-datum for an environment-machine design: "Inferring everything this way cost init 4\%, and probing every binder for heaviness 6\%"}, because what is inferred of a closed (fvar-instantiated) term is shared across all occurrences at any depth, whereas what is inferred of an open term under an environment is not.}
\li{Projection types: pre-stripped field domain per structure; a field type that is a bare parameter is read off the spine (\code{\verb~|machine.py:11421-11462~}).}
\li{\code{\verb~|_cheap_beta~} on inferred lambda body types (only when the beta is free: body closed or a bare variable, \code{\verb~|machine.py:11302~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.9 Declaration admission}

\ul{
\li{\strong{def/theorem/opaque}: \code{\verb~|check_value~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:12690-12727~}): value closed; type's type whnf's to a sort (Prop for theorems); \code{\verb~|def_eq(type, infer_expected(value, type))~}. Theorem and opaque values are dropped after a successful check (\code{\verb~|objects.py:5411-5430~}, \code{\verb~|5385~}).}
\li{\strong{Ordering and safety} (\code{\verb~|TypeChecker.check_reference~}, \code{\verb~|environment.py:182-206~}; commit \code{\verb~|463a310~}): each declaration gets an \code{\verb~|index~}; a constant may refer only to earlier indices, except within its own group (an inductive block; an unsafe definition with its mutual block; a partial mutual block), with staged scoping inside inductive blocks (\code{\verb~|STAGE_PRE_BLOCK~}, \code{\verb~|STAGE_IND_ONLY~}); a referenced declaration may not be less safe. Arena tests fixed by this: \code{\verb~|014_selfProof~}, \code{\verb~|141_falseFromUnsafe~}, \code{\verb~|142_falseFromPartial~}.}
\li{\strong{Inductives}: recursors are \strong{regenerated and compared} (\code{\verb~|_inductive.py~}: \code{\verb~|collect_members~} incl. nested occurrences as extra block members, \code{\verb~|check_types~}, \code{\verb~|check_constructors~} with strict positivity and universe checks, \code{\verb~|init_elim_level~}, \code{\verb~|is_k_target~}, \code{\verb~|recursors~}; entry \code{\verb~|recursors_of~}, \code{\verb~|_inductive.py:1201-1234~}). A declared recursor must have a name the kernel would generate, the same universe params, counts and K flag, and type and rule RHSs \code{\verb~|alpha_eq~} to the generated ones, falling back to "well-typed and def_eq" (\code{\verb~|objects.py:6199-6345~}). On init-prelude, Std and Mathlib all recursors were alpha-equal without the fallback (commit \code{\verb~|a31ca02~}). A constructor must be listed on its inductive (\code{\verb~|objects.py:6066-6080~}).}
\li{\strong{Quot}: names, universe arities, prerequisites (\code{\verb~|Quot~} before \code{\verb~|mk/lift/ind~}; \code{\verb~|Eq~} with \code{\verb~|Eq.refl~} of the prelude shape for \code{\verb~|lift~}) and def_eq of each type against the canonical signature (\code{\verb~|objects.py:5485-5750~}; commit \code{\verb~|076fbf8~}, arena \code{\verb~|bugs/quot-bad-type~}).}
\li{\strong{Axioms}: accepted if the type is a sort (\code{\verb~|objects.py:5455-5466~}); no allow-list. \code{\verb~|Lean.reduceBool~}/\code{\verb~|reduceNat~}/\code{\verb~|trustCompiler~} are not special-cased anywhere (grep finds no occurrence) ⇒ such constants are opaque and proofs needing native reduction fail def_eq and are rejected.}
\li{Loose bvars and undeclared universe params are rejected (\code{\verb~|LooseBoundVariable~}, \code{\verb~|UndeclaredLevelParam~}; commit \code{\verb~|8b20c3a~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.10 The closed-term CEK machine and the JIT (\code{\verb~|_eval.py~})}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Trigger}: only steps (a) of §1.7 and Nat-op argument evaluation; disabled under tracing. Any stuck neutral, opaque constant, free variable, K-recursor on a non-constructor, or unsupported shape raises \code{\verb~|_EvalBail~} and the ordinary machine continues (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:2003-2031~}).}
\li{\strong{Compilation}: a per-\code{\verb~|Environment~} \code{\verb~|CodeCache~} compiles \code{\verb~|W_Expr~}/handles once into immutable \code{\verb~|CodeNode~} graphs (\code{\verb~|CVal, CBVar, CLam, CApp(fn, args[]) (flattened spine), CLet, CProj, CCtor, CFullCtor, CDef (lazy body), CRec (rules pre-resolved), CNatOp, CQuotLift, COpaque~}; \code{\verb~|_eval.py:481-703~}, \code{\verb~|969-1389~}). Types and constructor \em{parameters are erased} at compile time; 0-field constructors are shared singletons; 1- and 2-field constructors have dedicated classes without arrays; the 14 Nat ops are first-class native closures so "typeclass-dispatched arithmetic never unfolds to unary \code{\verb~|Nat.brecOn~}"; small Nats are unboxed machine words (\code{\verb~|VSmallNat~}).}
\li{\strong{Machine}: state \code{\verb~|(code, env, args, cont)~}; \code{\verb~|Env~} = immutable linked list of slots (de Bruijn); a slot is a \code{\verb~|Val~} or a \code{\verb~|Thunk{code, env, val}~} updated in place when forced (call-by-need); continuations \code{\verb~|KUpdate, KProj, KRecMajor, KNatOp1/2, KNatSucc, KQuotLift~} (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:314-476~}, loop \code{\verb~|1568-1998~}). \code{\verb~|Nat.rec~} on a literal builds a lazy \code{\verb~|RecNatThunk~} for the IH.}
\li{\strong{JIT}: \code{\verb~|JitDriver(greens=['rec_edge', 'code'], reds=['steps','env','args','cont','cache','tc'])~} (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:1421-1426~}); \code{\verb~|jit_merge_point~} at the top of the loop (\code{\verb~|1578~}); \strong{\code{\verb~|can_enter_jit~} only on true recursive back-edges} — after an iota step on a recursive rule or \code{\verb~|Nat.rec~} on \code{\verb~|n > 0~} lands on the minor premise (\code{\verb~|rec_edge~} flag set at \code{\verb~|1827-1850~}, \code{\verb~|1894~}; consumed at \code{\verb~|1654-1658~}, \code{\verb~|1762-1776~}; \code{\verb~|can_enter_jit~} at \code{\verb~|1994~}). \code{\verb~|jit.promote~} on the code pointer of forced thunks, closure lambdas, constructor nodes, recursor nodes, projection indices (\code{\verb~|1753-1980~}); \code{\verb~|_immutable_fields_~} everywhere, quasi-immutable \code{\verb~|body?~}/\code{\verb~|is_compiled?~} on \code{\verb~|CDef~}; \code{\verb~|@jit.elidable~} on \code{\verb~|CRec.rule_index~}; \code{\verb~|@jit.unroll_safe~} on the small arg/field loops; \code{\verb~|@jit.dont_look_inside~} on compilation, bigint ops and environment lookups deeper than 8. No virtualizables; the linked \code{\verb~|Env~}/\code{\verb~|ArgNode~}/\code{\verb~|Cont~} objects rely on the tracer's allocation removal. No thresholds or trace limits are set in the source (RPython defaults apply; \code{\verb~|--jit~} passes user parameters through, \code{\verb~|_rlib/rcli.py:52-57~}). Warm-up cost is kept small structurally: nothing enters the machine unless a closed term meets a scalar, and nothing is counted as hot except recursor back-edges.}
\li{\strong{Measured} (commit \code{\verb~|dd8949e~}): \code{\verb~|perf/magma-list-deep-n36~} 113.8 B instr / 64.5 s / 13.5 GB → 1.81 B / 0.11 s / 94 MB, of which "12.4× from the JIT alone vs 22.4B with \code{\verb~|--jit off~}"; \code{\verb~|perf/beta-ladder~} 3.51 B → 0.28 B; \code{\verb~|perf/grind-ring-5~} 5.90 B → 5.08 B. The interpreter-level change (call-by-need machine, erased params, native Nat) is worth ~5× and the JIT a further ~12× on these loop-heavy tests; neither moves library totals.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.11 Scheduling, warm reuse, memory management}

\ul{
\li{No parallelism. The unit of work is one declaration, in file order.}
\li{\strong{One machine reused for all declarations} (commit \code{\verb~|7af8244~}, −5\% instructions on init/std): reset cost is proportional to what was used (zero the used prefix of memo/leaf arrays; delete consing entries record by record unless > 1/16 full, then memset; \code{\verb~|machine.py:1306-1433~}), tables grown by one huge declaration are given back above \code{\verb~|_STORE_KEEP_CAP = 2¹⁸~} records.}
\li{\p{\strong{Warm cross-declaration caches} (\code{\verb~|acquire~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:12809-12867~}; commits \code{\verb~|b9a7d66~}: NSE −25.8\% wall; \code{\verb~|ea2606b~}: thresholds doubled, NSE −8.0\%; \code{\verb~|85a2dc4~}: −2.3\%): for consecutive standalone def/theorem/opaque declarations of the same environment, arriving in increasing index order, the store is \strong{not reset} while it stays below \code{\verb~|_WARM_MAX_RECS = 196 608~} records, 65 536 leaves and 131 072 eqv/neq/failed entries (\code{\verb~|machine.py:452-457~}, \code{\verb~|7496-7507~}). Pure memos (whnf, whnf_core, infer in non-check mode, union-find, neq, import) stay valid because the environment only grows. Check-mode results are re-validated by bumping \code{\verb~|check_gen~}, except (i) consecutive \em{safe} declarations whose universe-parameter set includes the previous one's share a generation, and (ii) closed, level-param-free, safe sub-terms referencing only earlier declarations get the permanent stamp \code{\verb~|_CHECKED_PERM~} (\code{\verb~|machine.py:458-462~}, \code{\verb~|10238-10246~}, \code{\verb~|10469-10476~}). A rejection under a warm machine is \strong{re-checked on a cold machine} before being reported (\code{\verb~|environment.py:480-487~}).}
\pre{\verb~|
acquire(decl):                                                     # machine.py:12809-12867
  warmable = decl is standalone def/thm/opaque (group < 0, has an index) and no tracing and no memory limit
  if warmable and spare machine exists and same Environment and decl.index >= machine.lastIndex
     and store.nrecs < 196608 and nleaves < 65536 and eqv/neq/failed < 131072 each:
       if decl is safe and previous cohort was safe and prev.levelParams ⊆ decl.levelParams:
            keep check_gen                                         # verified subterms stay verified
       else check_gen += 1                                         # re-run reference/level/safety checks lazily
       can_perm = decl is safe;  decl_start_recs = store.nrecs;  open_memo.clear()
       return machine                                              # whnf / infer / eqv / neq / import memos stay
  else: machine.reset() (cost ∝ used entries);  check_gen = 1;  return machine
release(machine, failed): if failed or not warm-ready: reset
~}}
\li{Memory: live GC heap = names, levels, types of all declarations, values of definitions, plus AST nodes not yet released by the refcount protocol; the kernel working set is unmanaged and bounded by the caps above except for a single huge declaration. Bounded caches: \code{\verb~|_neq~}/\code{\verb~|_failed~} 4 M slots × 8 B ("cutting mathlib peak memory footprint from 11.02 GiB to 6.53 GiB", commit \code{\verb~|aeae8c5~}), substitution memos 2¹⁸ slots, \code{\verb~|_open_memo~} capped. Removing the process-global \code{\verb~|W_App~}/\code{\verb~|W_Proj~}/\code{\verb~|W_Let~} intern dicts: "full Mathlib now peaks at 9.61 GiB / 6.31 GiB RSS" (commit \code{\verb~|8b20c3a~}); arena reports 4.4 GB at the pin.}
\li{GC: RPython incminimark (generational, incremental major). The nursery estimate is floored at \strong{32 MB} at translation time (\code{\verb~|targetrpylean.py:14-46~}): "cuts wall time ~29\% on our benchmarks vs the 4 MB auto-estimate, and plateaus from there". \code{\verb~|PYPY_GC_*~} variables are used only for diagnostics in the history (\code{\verb~|PYPY_GC_MAJOR_COLLECT=1.1~} for true-live probes, commits \code{\verb~|abcef98~}, \code{\verb~|f724408~}); the arena run command sets none.}
\li{Stack: at start the process raises \code{\verb~|RLIMIT_STACK~} towards 1 GiB (as far as the hard limit allows) and re-\code{\verb~|exec~}s itself once, then sizes RPython's stack budget and shadow stack from the real limit (\code{\verb~|_stack.py~}, \code{\verb~|targetrpylean.py:84-88~}). Recursive walkers call \code{\verb~|stack_almost_full()~} every 32 frames (\code{\verb~|(rdepth & 31) == 31~}) and raise \code{\verb~|W_DeepRecursion~} — reported as a \em{rejection} of the declaration.}
}

\p{Thresholds in one place (all from \code{\verb~|machine.py~} unless noted):}

\table{
\tr{\th{Constant}\th{Value}\th{Meaning}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_WARM_MAX_RECS~} / \code{\verb~|_WARM_MAX_LEAVES~} / \code{\verb~|_WARM_MAX_EQV,NEQ,FAILED~}}\td{196 608 / 65 536 / 131 072}\td{store stays warm below these (\code{\verb~|:452-457~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_STORE_KEEP_CAP~}}\td{2¹⁸ records}\td{capacity kept across resets (\code{\verb~|:452~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_OPEN_RECORDS~}, \code{\verb~|_HEAVY~}}\td{2¹⁷ records since declaration start, 256 nodes}\td{switch to substitution-free inference (\code{\verb~|:497-501~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_MEMO_LIMIT~}}\td{2¹⁸ slots}\td{persistent substitution memos, wiped when full (\code{\verb~|:506~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_neq~}, \code{\verb~|_failed~} limit}\td{2²² slots × 8 B}\td{negative caches, wiped when full (\code{\verb~|:7467-7469~})}}
\tr{\td{app / other consing key width}\td{21 / 20 bits per handle}\td{above: promote table to wide entries (\code{\verb~|:354-357~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_LGEN_SIZE~}}\td{512}\td{direct-mapped (level params, levels) → generation cache (\code{\verb~|:362~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_BVAR_ARR_LEN~}}\td{256}\td{bvar leaves by index (\code{\verb~|:361~})}}
\tr{\td{Prop mask width}\td{62 argument positions}\td{(\code{\verb~|objects.py:4595~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|inst_eq~} budget}\td{512 steps}\td{(\code{\verb~|:3125~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_proj_lazy_eq~} budget}\td{8 unfolds, depth 3 (2 for extra args)}\td{(\code{\verb~|:11943-11945~}, \code{\verb~|:11982~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_LAZY_DELTA_MAX_ITER~}}\td{100 000}\td{(\code{\verb~|:7443~})}}
\tr{\td{stack probe period}\td{every 32 recursive frames}\td{(\code{\verb~|:2506~}, \code{\verb~|:7765~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_REDUCE_POW_MAX_EXP~}}\td{2²⁴}\td{native \code{\verb~|Nat.pow~} / \code{\verb~|shiftLeft~} decline above (\code{\verb~|objects.py:3425~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_CONST_CACHE_SIZE~}}\td{65 536}\td{direct-mapped \code{\verb~|W_Const~} cache (\code{\verb~|objects.py:1033~})}}
\tr{\td{parse chunk}\td{262 144 bytes}\td{(\code{\verb~|parser.py:2732~})}}
\tr{\td{GC nursery floor}\td{32 MB}\td{(\code{\verb~|targetrpylean.py:38~})}}
\tr{\td{stack wanted}\td{1 GiB via \code{\verb~|RLIMIT_STACK~} + re-exec}\td{(\code{\verb~|_stack.py:18~})}}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.12 Soundness-sensitive or fragile short-cuts — do not copy blindly}

\ol{
\li{\strong{Theorems are never delta-unfolded; their values are freed after checking.} The official kernel can unfold theorems (\code{\verb~|constant_info::has_value~} is \code{\verb~|is_theorem() || is_definition()~}, \code{\verb~|lean4/src/kernel/declaration.h:447-449~}, used by \code{\verb~|is_delta~}, \code{\verb~|lean4/src/kernel/type_checker.cpp:551-559~}). rpylean tried theorem delta (commit \code{\verb~|fb4c26a~}) and reverted it (commit \code{\verb~|f484d44~}) because it broke other Mathlib proofs in \em{its} strategy. Outcome can only be a wrong rejection, not a wrong acceptance, and Mathlib passes — but a proof that needs a theorem's body unfolded would be rejected. RLVM should keep theorem bodies re-materialisable (tenet-jvm does: lazily rebuilt from its compact store).}
\li{\strong{Structure eta of a recursor's stuck major is applied even when the structure is a proposition} (\code{\verb~|_to_cnstr_when_structure~}, \code{\verb~|machine.py:9448-9496~}, no Prop test; commit \code{\verb~|f484d44~} "drops the Prop guard"), whereas the reference at v4.36 returns early for propositions (\code{\verb~|lean4/src/kernel/inductive.h:61-72~}). This is how rpylean reduces \code{\verb~|And.casesOn h (…) : Rat~} without unfolding the theorem \code{\verb~|h~}. It manufactures projections \code{\verb~|h.i~} out of Prop structures; illegal ones (data field of a Prop structure) raise in \code{\verb~|_infer_proj~} if their type is ever inferred. Per tenet-jvm's notes the reference itself changed this area in 4.37 (§2.6) \strong{\verb~|[~unverified against lean4 master\verb~|]~}. Treat as version-dependent behaviour to be decided deliberately.}
\li{\strong{Prop-argument masks.} Sound only if (i) the mask is exactly right for the instantiated head type, (ii) both applications are well-typed, (iii) all earlier arguments were found def-eq (so the two proofs have def-eq types). rpylean enforces (iii) by left-to-right order and (ii) by enabling masks only while checking a declaration; (i) rests on ~130 lines of syntactic analysis plus level "plans" (\code{\verb~|objects.py:4651-4967~}). An over-approximate mask is a soundness hole (unequal data arguments skipped). If copied: derive the mask by actual inference with fvars (rpylean's dynamic fallback, \code{\verb~|machine.py:7604-7665~}) or validate the static analysis against it in tests.}
\li{\strong{Warm caches across declarations.} Equivalence classes, negative results and inferred types computed while checking declaration \em{n} are trusted for \em{n+1}. Sound because def_eq/whnf/infer(non-check) depend only on already-admitted declarations and handles are canonical — but it requires that \em{nothing} declaration-specific leaks into those memos: universe-parameter validity, reference ordering and safety are exactly the things re-validated per \code{\verb~|check_gen~}. \code{\verb~|_CHECKED_PERM~} additionally assumes monotone declaration order. Only failures are cross-checked cold; a wrong acceptance from a stale memo would go unnoticed.}
\li{\strong{Canonical fvars shared between binders with identical (record, domain)} — sound because a closed binder record cannot contain itself and the fvar's type is the domain; the old object kernel had a real bug of this family when binders were interned ("\code{\verb~|∀ p p, Eq p p~} checks even where the declared signature was \code{\verb~|∀ p a, Eq p a~}", \code{\verb~|objects.py:1342-1349~}).}
\li{\strong{Negative def_eq cache} and \strong{bounded heuristics} (\code{\verb~|_proj_lazy_eq~} budget 8/depth 3, \code{\verb~|inst_eq~} budget 512, lazy-delta iteration cap 100 000): each must fail \em{open} (fall through to the complete procedure). They do in the code read; the iteration cap returns UNDEF, not false.}
\li{\strong{Untyped CEK evaluation}: parameters and types are erased and K-like reduction is not performed there (bail instead). Any divergence between its reduction rules and the kernel's is a soundness risk confined to \code{\verb~|decide~}-style goals; rpylean returns the scalar as a \em{handle that then goes through the normal comparison}.}
\li{Resource failures are verdicts: deep recursion ⇒ reject (exit 1). For the arena a wrongly rejected good proof is ranking criterion 2, so RLVM should prefer not to convert resource exhaustion into "reject" \strong{\verb~|[~inference; scoring details owned by the arena research doc\verb~|]~}.}
\li{Historical bugs that the arena caught in rpylean and that are cheap to test for: level order accepted \code{\verb~|1 ≤ imax (u+1) v~} (commit \code{\verb~|6a33667~}); \code{\verb~|imax~} not collapsing to \code{\verb~|max~} when the right side is never zero (9 Mathlib false rejections, commit \code{\verb~|c126c31~}); recursors checked for shape only (commit \code{\verb~|a31ca02~}); argument checks performed inside def_eq-internal inference rejected valid terms with beta-redex domains (13+ Mathlib declarations, commit \code{\verb~|68de64f~}); \code{\verb~|is_prop~} compared the sort syntactically instead of after whnf (commit \code{\verb~|cf55c56~}); the same-head args shortcut must be limited to \em{regular} definitions, not abbrevs (commit \code{\verb~|8072e12~}); failing a same-class structural comparison must still try eta/struct-eta (commit \code{\verb~|34dc110~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.13 Build-level}

\p{\code{\verb~|pypy rpython --opt=jit --output=rpylean-c targetrpylean.py~} (\code{\verb~|rpylean/justfile:59~}); the arena build clones PyPy for the toolchain (\code{\verb~|lean-kernel-arena/checkers/rpylean.yaml~}). No PGO, LTO or target-cpu flags appear; the C is whatever RPython's default makefile produces \strong{\verb~|[~flags not inspected\verb~|]~}. The micro-tuning that replaces PGO is manual: \code{\verb~|@always_inline~} on accessors, \code{\verb~|@dont_inline~} on every miss/slow path so that hit paths compile to leaf functions without callee-saved spills (commits \code{\verb~|aeae8c5~}, \code{\verb~|90d0b58~}: "\code{\verb~|Machine.def_eq~} (8 inst), \code{\verb~|Machine.whnf~} (16 inst)"), packing live values to cut ARM64 stack spills (commit \code{\verb~|7e11d57~}: 115 → 62 spills, −1.1\% instructions), \code{\verb~|zero=False~} allocation of write-before-read arrays, tuple-free returns through out-fields.}
}

