}

\subtree{
\title{1.15 RPython mechanism → Truffle/Graal equivalent}

\table{
\tr{\th{RPython (where used in rpylean)}\th{Purpose}\th{Truffle / Graal / HotSpot equivalent}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|JitDriver(greens=[rec_edge, code], reds=[…])~}, \code{\verb~|jit_merge_point~} (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:1421, 1578~})}\td{meta-trace the CEK loop keyed on the Lean code position}\td{One Truffle \code{\verb~|RootNode~}/\code{\verb~|CallTarget~} per compiled Lean definition or rule RHS; \code{\verb~|CodeNode~} → \code{\verb~|Node~} subclasses with \code{\verb~|execute~}; compilation is per call target (method-based partial evaluation) rather than per trace}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|can_enter_jit~} only at recursor back-edges (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:1994~})}\td{count hotness only where loops are}\td{Call-count / loop-count thresholds (\code{\verb~|engine.FirstTierCompilationThreshold~}, \code{\verb~|engine.LastTierCompilationThreshold~}), \code{\verb~|LoopNode~} + OSR for self-recursion through IHs; keep cold code in the interpreter}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|jit.promote(x)~} (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:1753-1980~})}\td{make a runtime value a guarded trace constant}\td{Inline cache: \code{\verb~|@Specialization(guards = "code == cachedCode", limit = "N")~} with \code{\verb~|@Cached~}; \code{\verb~|DirectCallNode~} vs \code{\verb~|IndirectCallNode~}; \code{\verb~|CompilerDirectives.isPartialEvaluationConstant~} for assertions}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|_immutable_fields_~}, \code{\verb~|fields[*]~}}\td{let the JIT fold reads from constant objects}\td{\code{\verb~|final~} fields, \code{\verb~|@CompilationFinal~}, \code{\verb~|@CompilationFinal(dimensions = 1)~} arrays, \code{\verb~|@Child~}/\code{\verb~|@Children~}}}
\tr{\td{quasi-immutable \code{\verb~|'body?'~}, \code{\verb~|'is_compiled?'~} (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:607~}), \code{\verb~|'tracer?'~} (\code{\verb~|environment.py:281~})}\td{field treated as constant; a write invalidates compiled code}\td{\code{\verb~|@CompilationFinal~} + \code{\verb~|CompilerDirectives.transferToInterpreterAndInvalidate()~} on write, or an \code{\verb~|Assumption~} checked in compiled code}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|@jit.elidable~} (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:659~}, \code{\verb~|objects.py:67~})}\td{pure call folded when arguments are constants}\td{methods on PE-constant receivers fold automatically; otherwise \code{\verb~|@TruffleBoundary~} + cache in a \code{\verb~|@CompilationFinal~} field}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|@jit.unroll_safe~} (\code{\verb~|_eval.py:1464-1531~})}\td{unroll loops with small constant trip counts}\td{\code{\verb~|@ExplodeLoop~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|@jit.dont_look_inside~}}\td{residual call, opaque to the tracer}\td{\code{\verb~|@TruffleBoundary~}}}
\tr{\td{allocation removal of \code{\verb~|Env~}/\code{\verb~|ArgNode~}/\code{\verb~|Cont~} (no virtualizables are used)}\td{keep interpreter state in registers}\td{Graal partial escape analysis; \code{\verb~|VirtualFrame~} slots for locals instead of linked environments}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|lltype.malloc(flavor='raw')~} arrays (\code{\verb~|machine.py:186-326~})}\td{data the GC never traces or moves}\td{\code{\verb~|int[]~}/\code{\verb~|long[]~} (a primitive array has no references, so the collector never scans its contents; it may still be copied while young, so allocate the big ones once and keep them) or off-heap \code{\verb~|MemorySegment~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|@always_inline~} / \code{\verb~|@dont_inline~} hit/miss splitting}\td{leaf-function fast paths}\td{small hot methods + out-of-line slow paths. HotSpot C2 inlines by bytecode size (\code{\verb~|MaxInlineSize=35~}, \code{\verb~|FreqInlineSize=325~} defaults); the Graal compiler uses its own heuristics, so verify with compilation logs. \code{\verb~|HostCompilerDirectives.InliningCutoff~} for Truffle host code}}
\tr{\td{nursery floor via patched \code{\verb~|estimate_best_nursery_size~} (\code{\verb~|targetrpylean.py~})}\td{fewer minor GCs}\td{\code{\verb~|-Xmn~} / \code{\verb~|-XX:NewSize~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|rstack.stack_almost_full()~} + re-exec with larger \code{\verb~|RLIMIT_STACK~}}\td{deep recursion}\td{checker thread with explicit large stack size (tenet-jvm \code{\verb~|Main.java:31-41~}); catch \code{\verb~|StackOverflowError~} at the declaration boundary}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|rbigint~}, unboxed \code{\verb~|VSmallNat~}}\td{Nat literals}\td{\code{\verb~|long~} fast path with \code{\verb~|Math.*Exact~}, \code{\verb~|BigInteger~} slow path}}
\tr{\td{identity dicts on interned \code{\verb~|Name~}; inline cache fields \code{\verb~|Name._decl_cached~}}\td{no hashing on hot lookups}\td{put the data in a field of the interned object; avoid \code{\verb~|HashMap~}/\code{\verb~|IdentityHashMap~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|compute_identity_hash~} was 14\% of samples (commit \code{\verb~|9ef360d~})}\td{—}\td{avoid \code{\verb~|System.identityHashCode~} in hot paths; explicit \code{\verb~|int id~} field}}
\tr{\td{weak-dict interning, maps/shapes}\td{\strong{not used} in rpylean}\td{—}}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.16 What RLVM cannot get from Truffle here}

\p{The kernel's hot loops (\code{\verb~|cons_app~}, \code{\verb~|_inst_*~}, \code{\verb~|whnf_core~}, \code{\verb~|def_eq~}) operate on \em{data} (handles whose kinds vary unpredictably), not on a program with a stable position to specialise on. rpylean's measurement (finding 2) says a trace/PE compiler has nothing to fold there and its bookkeeping costs ~15-19\%. On the JVM these loops should be ordinary Java, kept monomorphic (switch on an \code{\verb~|int~} kind, no virtual dispatch, no boxing), compiled once by the top-tier compiler — and since compiler threads are billed, the size and number of hot methods is a budget item. Truffle belongs where rpylean put its JIT: evaluating closed Lean code (\code{\verb~|decide~}, \code{\verb~|Nat.rec~}/\code{\verb~|List.rec~} loops, recursor-heavy reflection), behind an explicit boundary, entered rarely.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{2. tenet-jvm post-mortem (what not to do on the JVM)}

\subtree{
\title{2.1 Facts}

\ul{
\li{Arena: 27.2 min virtual = \strong{9.79e12 instructions}, 11.8 GB, single checker thread (\code{\verb~|lean-kernel-arena/checkers/tenet-jvm.yaml~}: \code{\verb~|build: make~}, \code{\verb~|run: bin/tenet-jvm "$IN"~}). Its README reports 30.1 min wall on the arena runner and 14-19 min on an Apple-silicon laptop with \code{\verb~|-Xmx9g~}.}
\li{~3 500 lines of plain Java, no dependencies, compiled by \code{\verb~|javac~} (\code{\verb~|Makefile~}). Launcher (\code{\verb~|bin/tenet-jvm:5~}): \code{\verb~|java ${JAVA_OPTS:--XX:+UseParallelGC -XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75} -cp out tenet.Main~}.}
\li{It is a faithful port of the reference algorithm (substitution-based, locally nameless, \code{\verb~|HashMap~} caches), by design: "matching its decisions is what makes an independent implementation useful as a cross-check" (\code{\verb~|docs/design.md~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{2.2 Architecture (at \code{\verb~|4cc6e20~})}

\p{\code{\verb~|ExportReader~} (line → \code{\verb~|Json.parse~} → \code{\verb~|Map~}) → \code{\verb~|ExprStore~} (flat \code{\verb~|byte[] kind~}, \code{\verb~|int[] a,b,c,d~}: ~17 B/node; expressions become \code{\verb~|Expr~} objects on demand via a memo) → \code{\verb~|Kernel.add~} → \code{\verb~|TypeChecker~} (infer / whnfCore / whnf / isDefEq / lazy delta) and \code{\verb~|InductiveChecker~} + \code{\verb~|NestedInductive~} (regenerate recursors, compare). Theorem values are built into a scratch memo and released after checking but can be rebuilt from the store (\code{\verb~|Decl.Thm.value()~}, \code{\verb~|Decl.java:44-72~}), so theorems remain unfoldable.}
}

\subtree{
\title{2.3 Where instructions and memory go (structural; no profile is published, so shares are \strong{\verb~|[~unverified\verb~|]~})}

\p{Parsing — every one of the >100 M lines:}

\ol{
\li{\code{\verb~|BufferedReader.readLine()~} decodes UTF-8 into a fresh \code{\verb~|String~} (\code{\verb~|ExportReader.java:101~}).}
\li{\code{\verb~|Json.parse(line)~} builds a generic tree: a \code{\verb~|LinkedHashMap<String,Object>~} per object (two per \code{\verb~|app~} line), a \code{\verb~|StringBuilder~} + new \code{\verb~|String~} \strong{for every key} ("app", "fn", "arg", "ie" are re-allocated and re-hashed on every line), boxed \code{\verb~|Long~} per number, \code{\verb~|ArrayList~} per array (\code{\verb~|Json.java:40, 75, 99~}).}
\li{Dispatch by a chain of \code{\verb~|containsKey~} probes: an \code{\verb~|app~} line pays "meta", "in", "il", "ie", then "bvar", "sort", "const", "app" (\code{\verb~|ExportReader.java:120-170~}).}
}

\p{Contrast: rpylean handles the same line with three 8-byte compares and three integer parses.}

\p{Term objects and equality:}

\<html:ol>[start]{4}{
\<html:li>{\code{\verb~|Expr~} nodes are heap objects with five header fields (\code{\verb~|kind~} enum ref, \code{\verb~|hash~}, \code{\verb~|looseBVarRange~}, two booleans) plus children (\code{\verb~|Expr.java:14-30~}); "roughly 45 bytes" each by the author's estimate (\code{\verb~|ExprStore.java~} class comment).}
\<html:li>{Sharing is a \em{lossy} direct-mapped table of 2¹⁸ entries (\code{\verb~|Expr.java:162-188~}), so pointer equality is only probabilistic; every cache is therefore keyed by \strong{structural} \code{\verb~|equals~}: \code{\verb~|hash~} compare, then a recursive walk with a 256-step budget, then a second walk allocating a \code{\verb~|Pair~} per node into a \code{\verb~|HashSet~} using \code{\verb~|System.identityHashCode~} (\code{\verb~|Expr.java:194-240~}, \code{\verb~|293-339~}).}
\<html:li>{\code{\verb~|Name~} is not interned; \code{\verb~|equals~} walks the component chain comparing strings (\code{\verb~|Name.java:35-47~}); \code{\verb~|Env.get~} is \code{\verb~|HashMap<Name,Decl>.get~} (\code{\verb~|Env.java:8, 30~}) and is called for every head constant in \code{\verb~|whnfCore~}, \code{\verb~|deltaInfo~}, \code{\verb~|reduceRecursor~}, \code{\verb~|reduceProj~}, structure-eta.}
}

\p{Checker caches:}

\<html:ol>[start]{7}{
\<html:li>{Seven hash containers per declaration: \code{\verb~|Map<Expr,Expr>~} ×5 (+ \code{\verb~|deltaStepCache~}), \code{\verb~|Set<List<Expr>>~} ×2 (\code{\verb~|TypeChecker.java:33-39, 527~}); each entry is a \code{\verb~|HashMap.Node~} (≈32-48 B) and each pair lookup allocates \code{\verb~|List.of(t, s)~} (\code{\verb~|TypeChecker.java:635, 642, 901~}). They are re-allocated per declaration when larger than 256 entries (\code{\verb~|TypeChecker.java:43-63~}). The author notes that caching cheap \code{\verb~|whnfCore~} results "grows to tens of millions of entries on large Mathlib declarations and the checker ends up in GC" (comment at \code{\verb~|TypeChecker.java:302-304~}) — the JVM-specific failure mode of object-per-entry caches.}
\<html:li>{No union-find over proven equalities ("EquivManager reverted", commit \code{\verb~|07e3d63~}); at the pinned revision def_eq failures are cached only for the same-head case. The later commit \code{\verb~|53cf8a4~} added a general failure cache after one 226-node proof ran "25 min at 104 GB".}
\<html:li>{Fresh free variables on every binder opening: \code{\verb~|long id = ++fvarCounter; lctx.put(id, new Local(…))~} with \code{\verb~|Map<Long, Local>~} (boxing) (\code{\verb~|TypeChecker.java:26, 31, 69-73~}). Instantiated bodies are therefore new terms each time and no cache entry from a previous opening can hit (rpylean's canonical fvars exist precisely to avoid this).}
}

\p{Substitution and spines:}

\<html:ol>[start]{10}{
\<html:li>{One generic \code{\verb~|replace(e, Replacer f)~} taking a lambda (\code{\verb~|Expr.java:371-474~}); all of instantiate / lift / lower / abstract / level-instantiate go through the same megamorphic \code{\verb~|f.apply(e, off)~} call site. Small terms are walked without a memo; after 4 096 steps a preallocated exception restarts the walk with a \code{\verb~|HashMap<Key,Expr>~} (a \code{\verb~|Key~} object and \code{\verb~|identityHashCode~} per node) — the first 4 096 steps are wasted.}
\<html:li>{\code{\verb~|getAppArgs()~} allocates an array \em{and} an \code{\verb~|ArrayList~} per call (\code{\verb~|Expr.java:356-364~}) and is called on every \code{\verb~|whnfCore~} of an application, every recursor/projection reduction and every \code{\verb~|isDefEqApp~}; \code{\verb~|args.subList(…).toArray(new Expr[0])~} in inference (\code{\verb~|TypeChecker.java:180-214~}). Level instantiation of a definition body is cached per constant (\code{\verb~|unfoldCache~}) but of a constant's \em{type} is not (\code{\verb~|inferConst~} re-instantiates, \code{\verb~|TypeChecker.java:136-146~}).}
}

\p{Memory and GC:}

\<html:ol>[start]{12}{
\<html:li>{At the pin, types and definition bodies stay materialised as \code{\verb~|Expr~} objects for the whole run in \code{\verb~|keptMemo~} (\code{\verb~|ExprStore.java:153-158~}) on top of the flat store.}
\<html:li>{\code{\verb~|-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75~} ⇒ a 12 GB heap limit on the 16 GB runner; with a throughput collector the heap simply grows to the limit before full collections reclaim it, so the reported 11.8 GB is the \em{limit}, not the need (the author measures a live heap of 2.86 GB for a 42.3 M-expression Mathlib slice at the pinned design and 1.16 GB after commit \code{\verb~|f210e4d~}). \code{\verb~|-XX:+UseParallelGC~} runs one GC worker per CPU; under the arena metric every worker's instructions, including work-stealing spin, are billed \strong{\verb~|[~inference; the GC share was not measured\verb~|]~}.}
\<html:li>{Recursion: a 4 GiB-stack thread (\code{\verb~|Main.java:41~}); \code{\verb~|StackOverflowError~} inside one declaration is caught and counted as a \em{rejection} of that declaration (\code{\verb~|Main.java:75-82~}); \code{\verb~|OutOfMemoryError~} ⇒ exit 3.}
}

\p{What happened after the pin (HEAD \code{\verb~|53cf8a4~}): chunked store at ~10.6 B/node, declarations hold ids, object memo dropped beyond 2²¹ nodes (commit \code{\verb~|f210e4d~}: live heap 2.86 → 1.16 GB, 282 → 263 s on the slice), failure cache with cold re-check (\code{\verb~|53cf8a4~}). The direction — ids and primitive arrays instead of objects — is the same one rpylean took, but the checker itself still works on \code{\verb~|Expr~} objects and \code{\verb~|HashMap~}s.}
}

\subtree{
\title{2.4 Worth copying}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Fail-closed verdict} (\code{\verb~|Main.java:29-44~}): exit code starts at 3; set to 0 only by a normal return after the whole file (non-empty, with a metadata record) was processed; every \code{\verb~|Throwable~} maps to non-zero; an empty input or a first line that is not the metadata record is a rejection (\code{\verb~|ExportReader.java:113, 116~}).}
\li{\strong{Large-stack checker thread}: \code{\verb~|new Thread(null, runnable, "checker", 4L << 30)~}; \code{\verb~|main~} only joins and exits. (Stack pages are committed on touch; a deep excursion stays resident afterwards.)}
\li{\strong{Derive, then compare} for inductives, including bookkeeping flags (\code{\verb~|isRec~}, \code{\verb~|isReflexive~}, \code{\verb~|numNested~}, \code{\verb~|k~}, \code{\verb~|cidx~}, \code{\verb~|numFields~}) and nested inductives via auxiliary types translated back (\code{\verb~|docs/design.md~}); counts and indices beyond 32 bits are refused rather than truncated (\code{\verb~|ExportReader.java:85-90~}); a loose bvar in an inductive declaration is refused up front.}
\li{\strong{Cold re-check of any rejection} when heuristics that can only cause false negatives were in play (HEAD) — same policy as rpylean's warm-machine re-check.}
\li{\strong{Explicit heap sizing rather than a percentage}: decide \code{\verb~|-Xmx~} from the measured live set. For RLVM: young generation sized explicitly (rpylean's nursery lesson), old generation small because the working set lives in primitive arrays, GC thread count fixed and small \strong{\verb~|[~recommendation, to be validated by instruction counts\verb~|]~}.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{2.5 Not worth copying}

\p{\code{\verb~|-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75~}; ParallelGC with default thread count; \code{\verb~|String~}-per-line parsing; any \code{\verb~|Map<String,Object>~}; object-per-term with structural-equality caches; \code{\verb~|HashMap~}s created per declaration; boxed keys; lambda-parameterised traversals on hot paths; \code{\verb~|List<Expr>~} argument lists; mapping \code{\verb~|StackOverflowError~} to "rejected".}
}

\subtree{
\title{2.6 Kernel-rule notes from tenet-jvm that RLVM must track (from \code{\verb~|docs/divergences.md~}, not independently verified against lean4 master)}

\ul{
\li{Lean \strong{4.37.0-rc1 changed three def_eq rules}, selected in tenet-jvm from the export's metadata version (\code{\verb~|LeanVersion.kernelHasEta437~}): (i) proof irrelevance is tried \em{before} the first \code{\verb~|whnfCore~} (lean4\verb~|#~15103); (ii) a recursor major that is a proof is not reduced, and structure-eta on the major is skipped only when the recursor has as many universe params as its inductive (so \code{\verb~|And.rec~} gets eta) (lean4\verb~|#~15371); (iii) structure eta against a \em{partially applied} constructor by applying both sides to fresh variables (lean4\verb~|#~15373). "Neither direction is the lenient one"; test exports \code{\verb~|tests/exports/eta437.ndjson~} and \code{\verb~|acc436.ndjson~} hold one direction each.}
\li{\code{\verb~|Nat~} literal arithmetic must \strong{not} refuse terms mentioning free variables inside \code{\verb~|reduce_nat~} (only the lazy-delta call site has that test): otherwise Lean 4.37's \code{\verb~|Nat.trailingZeros_rec_eq_bits~} compares two copies of 2⁶⁴ unarily.}
\li{"Is this level zero" must be decided up to equivalence (\code{\verb~|Sort (imax 1 0)~} is \code{\verb~|Prop~}; lean4\verb~|#~14613), and a type whose sort does not reduce to a \code{\verb~|Sort~} is an error rather than "not a proposition" (lean4\verb~|#~14807).}
\li{Level comparison bug class: \code{\verb~|u+2 ≥ 1~} decided false / \code{\verb~|3 ≥ u+1~} decided true by comparing offsets in the wrong case (commit \code{\verb~|21307e3~}) — found by the arena on navier-stokes-euler.}
\li{String literals expand through \code{\verb~|String.ofList~} when the environment has it, else \code{\verb~|String.mk~}.}
\li{\code{\verb~|isDefEqApp~} must compare arguments first-to-last ("a Mathlib declaration that ran for over 10 minutes now checks in about 3 s", commit \code{\verb~|7a40037~}).}
\li{Cheap and full \code{\verb~|whnfCore~} results must not be mixed in one cache (found on \code{\verb~|Int32~} range instances in Init).}
}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{3. Ranked tricks and their JVM/Truffle realisation}

\p{Ranking is by measured effect in rpylean's history, then by how directly tenet-jvm's cost profile is the absence of the trick.}

\table{
\tr{\th{\verb~|#~}\th{Trick}\th{Evidence}\th{Realisation in RLVM (allocation cheap; pointer chasing, megamorphism, boxing, GC tracing and JIT work are the costs)}}
\tr{\td{1}\td{Hash-consed term store in primitive arrays, int handles, per declaration}\td{init 4.1×, std 28× fewer instructions, 3.6× less memory (\code{\verb~|0866ac8~}, \code{\verb~|2ec1abf~}); GC tracing was ~45\% before (\code{\verb~|d3e30e2~})}\td{\code{\verb~|int[] recs~} (4 ints/record), \code{\verb~|long[] appTable~} with the packed \code{\verb~|(fn|arg|idx)~} entry, handles as \code{\verb~|int~} with the low-bit leaf tag. No \code{\verb~|Expr~} objects in the kernel. Growth by doubling+copy is fine below the warm cap; pre-size from the previous declaration}}
\tr{\td{2}\td{Memo slots parallel to records; union-find inside them; negative cache as a packed-\code{\verb~|long~} open-addressed set}\td{83\% identity hits, 86\% UF hits of the rest (\code{\verb~|4746484~}); capped sets cut Mathlib peak 11.0 → 6.5 GiB (\code{\verb~|aeae8c5~})}\td{\code{\verb~|int[] memos~} (6 per record), \code{\verb~|long[]~} sets; clearing = \code{\verb~|Arrays.fill~} of the used prefix. Zero objects per cache entry (tenet-jvm's \code{\verb~|HashMap.Node~} + \code{\verb~|List.of~} per lookup is the anti-pattern)}}
\tr{\td{3}\td{Prop-argument masks: skip proof arguments in same-head comparisons}\td{NSE −24.4\% instructions (\code{\verb~|c87c5b4~})}\td{one \code{\verb~|long~} per declaration (+ level-dependent plans); compute by real inference first, add the static analysis only with a cross-check (§1.12 item 3)}}
\tr{\td{4}\td{Warm caches across consecutive declarations with check generations; reuse of one machine}\td{NSE −25.8\% wall, then −8\%, −2.3\% (\code{\verb~|b9a7d66~}, \code{\verb~|ea2606b~}, \code{\verb~|85a2dc4~}); −5\% (\code{\verb~|7af8244~})}\td{keep arrays; bump an \code{\verb~|int~} generation instead of clearing; caps sized to stay cache-resident (rpylean: 196 608 records ≈ 13 MB). With parallel workers each worker has its own store ⇒ warm reuse per worker; file-order locality then matters for chunking}}
\tr{\td{5}\td{Lazy def_eq discipline: \code{\verb~|whnf_core~} never deltas; one delta layer per step; proof irrelevance before delta; same-head args only for regular hints; failure cache}\td{\code{\verb~|0a9a45d~}, \code{\verb~|8072e12~}: 25 init declarations from > 30 s to seconds}\td{algorithmic; language-independent}}
\tr{\td{6}\td{Fused import from the parsed AST: level substitution during import, generation-stamped intrusive memo, strip lambdas beta will discard, first-use level+argument fusion, shape-specialised unfolds (\code{\verb~|λ…BVar~}, \code{\verb~|λ…Proj~}) and iota (\code{\verb~|simple_minor~})}\td{Mathlib −7.2\% (\code{\verb~|5c6b8fe~}); NSE −3.4\% (\code{\verb~|90bc723~}), −5.2\% cycles (\code{\verb~|769f42b~})}\td{parsed terms as a compact persistent int store (tenet-jvm's \code{\verb~|ExprStore~} layout is right for this); per-worker import memo \code{\verb~|int[]~} indexed by export id + generation stamp instead of a field on a shared object; per-declaration precomputed "unfold plan" objects}}
\tr{\td{7}\td{One-shot epoch-stamped substitution memo + multi-argument instantiate from a spine buffer}\td{−10…−15\% (\code{\verb~|53c4861~})}\td{\code{\verb~|long[] callSlot~}; \code{\verb~|int[] spine~} used as an explicit stack; no \code{\verb~|List~}/varargs; recursion depth guard by counter}}
\tr{\td{8}\td{Compare-instead-of-instantiate (\code{\verb~|inst_eq~}), expected-type propagation, joint ∀/λ telescope check, pending-argument Pi walks}\td{NSE −7.3\%, cslib −5.9\% (\code{\verb~|8d7da87~}); \code{\verb~|d749f43~}, \code{\verb~|489f178~}}\td{same code shape; in a closure/NbE design this is "conversion-check a closure body against a value without quoting" — keep the idea whichever evaluator is chosen}}
\tr{\td{9}\td{Streaming parse interleaved with checking; refcount prescan to free terms at last use; drop (but keep re-materialisable) theorem bodies}\td{cslib 14.8 → 8.6 GB, 1.5× faster (\code{\verb~|1f6d220~})}\td{if the parsed export is kept as packed int arrays (≈11-17 B/node ⇒ ~1.2-1.8 GB for 107 M nodes) the prescan may be unnecessary; decide by peak-memory target}}
\tr{\td{10}\td{Fixed-shape SWAR parser for the three hot line shapes with a general fallback; in-place chunks}\td{−5…−6\% of total instructions (\code{\verb~|437cefa~}); footprint −50\% (\code{\verb~|291ae24~})}\td{\code{\verb~|byte[]~} chunks or a mapped \code{\verb~|MemorySegment~}; 8-byte little-endian loads via \code{\verb~|VarHandle~}/\code{\verb~|ByteBuffer.getLong~} compared with constants; hand-rolled integer parse; no \code{\verb~|String~} per line}}
\tr{\td{11}\td{Call-by-need CEK machine with compiled code for closed terms, JIT only there, entered only against Bool/Nat scalars}\td{12-63× on deep-reduction tests, ±0 on libraries (\code{\verb~|dd8949e~})}\td{the Truffle part of RLVM: nodes per \code{\verb~|CodeNode~} kind, call targets per definition/rule, thunks, erased params, unboxed small Nats, native Nat ops; high compilation thresholds; \code{\verb~|_EvalBail~} ⇒ fall back to the kernel}}
\tr{\td{12}\td{No JIT bookkeeping on kernel loops}\td{init 162.4 → 136.7 s when removed (\code{\verb~|1ba28a8~})}\td{kernel as plain Java behind \code{\verb~|@TruffleBoundary~}; measure total instructions including compiler threads; consider ahead-of-time compilation of the kernel if JIT cost is material \strong{\verb~|[~to be measured\verb~|]~}}}
\tr{\td{13}\td{Young-generation sizing}\td{−29\% wall from a 32 MB nursery (\code{\verb~|b6f3ab1~})}\td{\code{\verb~|-Xmn~} explicit; keep survivors rare by not retaining per-declaration objects}}
\tr{\td{14}\td{Per-name inline cache of the declaration; head classification flags + height in one int per leaf}\td{−4.8\% (\code{\verb~|7073bce~}); \code{\verb~|5af5b15~}}\td{\code{\verb~|Decl~} reference in the interned \code{\verb~|Name~}/constant object; \code{\verb~|int flags~} per leaf}}
\tr{\td{15}\td{Canonical fvars per (binder record, domain)}\td{prerequisite for memo hits under binders; absent in tenet-jvm (§2.3 item 9)}\td{\code{\verb~|long~}-keyed open-addressed map \code{\verb~|(binder, domain) → fvarLeaf~}}}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{4. What this says about the HOAS/NbE question}

\ul{
\li{rpylean reaches \verb~|#~4 \strong{without} NbE: substitution on a hash-consed store, with memoisation making each substitution linear in the DAG and with most substitutions avoided (§1.4, §1.8). The leaders above it are one substitution-based hash-consing checker (nano-lean) and one NbE checker with hash-consed values (gruszka), so on Mathlib the evaluator family is not the discriminator; cache identity and work avoidance are \strong{\verb~|[~inference from the leaderboard and the gain table\verb~|]~}.}
\li{rpylean's history contains a negative result about \em{closures without canonical identity}: \code{\verb~|W_Closure~} (deferred substitution, commits \code{\verb~|27874fd~}, \code{\verb~|0debdae~}, \code{\verb~|86da6e8~}, \code{\verb~|4619582~}) gave batched beta, but "the fresh identity-hashed closures it allocates per beta poison downstream \code{\verb~|W_App~} identity checks" and it was withdrawn (commit \code{\verb~|4c45e81~}); forcing the same closure repeatedly had to be memoised (commit \code{\verb~|e4f3ede~}: \code{\verb~|_instantiate_multi~} was ~45\% of a profile; 43.5 → 25.4 s) and the walk inside a force too (\code{\verb~|7fe61f7~}: → 8.0 s). \strong{An NbE/closure design must give values a canonical identity (hash-consed environments/values, or caches keyed on \code{\verb~|(code, env)~} handles); otherwise whnf/infer/def_eq memoisation — which resolves the large majority of calls — stops working.}}
\li{A second datum: environment-based inference (no substitution, \code{\verb~|_infer_open~}) was 4\% \em{slower} than substitution on init for ordinary terms because results on open terms are not shareable across depths (commit \code{\verb~|1f0405e~}); it wins by 70× only on deeply nested heavy terms. A hybrid (environment for deep/heavy terms, instantiate-and-share for light ones) is what rpylean ships.}
\li{Where rpylean does use an abstract machine with thunks (closed terms, §1.10), call-by-need plus erasure plus native Nat is worth ~5× before any JIT and the JIT ~12× more — exactly the workload where Truffle can pay for itself.}
\li{Many of rpylean's late optimisations (\code{\verb~|inst_eq~}, pending-argument Pi walks, first-use fusion, never importing discarded binder types) are substitution-world emulations of what closures provide natively (a body plus an environment that is never materialised unless needed). An NbE kernel gets these for free but must then solve the identity/caching problem above.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{5. Unverified / open}

\ul{
\li{Parse share of rpylean's Mathlib total and the final Mathlib instruction count on the authors' machine are not recorded (extrapolated ≈600 G on ARM64; arena 578 G on x86-64).}
\li{The C compiler flags RPython uses for the translated binary were not inspected.}
\li{tenet-jvm's split between parsing, GC, JIT and checking is not published; §2.3 lists mechanisms, not shares.}
\li{The lean4 4.37 rule changes (§2.6) are taken from tenet-jvm's documentation; \code{\verb~|refs/lean4~} is on the 4.36 line, where \code{\verb~|to_cnstr_when_structure~} still returns early for propositions.}
\li{Whether rpylean's Prop-mask static analysis is exactly equivalent to its inference-based fallback was not proven here; only its structure was read.}
}
}
